.TH DTLPSETUP 1 "2026-11-22" "Amiga UNIX add-on" "CDE"
.SH NAME
dtlpsetup \- print a file from the desktop (old name of dtlp)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dtlpsetup
.RB [ \-b
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR destination ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR command ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR copies ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR options ]
.RB [ \-u
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-a ]
.RB [ \-e ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-w ]
.B \-f
.I file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dtlpsetup
is the CDE 1.0 name of the desktop's print command.
It hands its options on to
.BR dtlp (1),
which prints
.IR file ;
each option means what it means to dtlp.
The CDE 1.0 options that dtlp does not have,
.BR \-c ,
.BR \-t ,
.B \-i
and
.BR \-l ,
are ignored; any other option, or an argument that is not an option,
gets the usage message.
.SH EXIT STATUS
dtlp's, except that its 5 and 6 are returned as 7 and 8, as CDE 1.0
returned them; 2 for a usage error.
.SH NOTES
The message that names ignored options is printed with
.BR dspmsg ,
which Amiga UNIX does not have; the shell reports it as not found, and
printing goes on.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dtlp (1),
.BR lp (1)
